{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"id":"WinDirStat.WinDirStat.Beta","latestVersion":"2.9.1.2026-10-04","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Disk usage statistics viewer and cleanup tool","license":"GPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/windirstat/windirstat/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.md","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Disk usage statistics viewer and cleanup tool","license":"GPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/windirstat/windirstat/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.md","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"WinDirStat is a program that allows you to find disk space hogs at a glance. It achieves that by displaying a drive, drives or directories in a treemap that assigns bigger areas to bigger files and directories. Making those areas visually separate by coloring and other means allows you to see literally at a glance what the space hogs are and where to dig deeper.\nThe directory tree is simultaneously shown as a tree list and as a treemap. One can effortlessly gain an impression of the proportions on the hard disk(s).\n\nMajor features\n  - Three views: Directory Tree, Treemap, and Extension\n  - Duplicate file detection\n  - Built-in cleanup actions including Open, Delete, Show Properties\n  - User-defined cleanup actions (command line based)","moniker":"windirstat-beta","name":"WinDirStat (Beta)","packageUrl":"https://windirstat.net/","publisher":"The WinDirStat Team","publisherUrl":"https://windirstat.net/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/windirstat/windirstat/releases/tag/beta/v2.9.1/2026-10-04","tags":["cleanup","disk-usage","kdirstat","organization","sequoiaview","statistics"]}},"longDescription":"WinDirStat is a program that allows you to find disk space hogs at a glance. It achieves that by displaying a drive, drives or directories in a treemap that assigns bigger areas to bigger files and directories. Making those areas visually separate by coloring and other means allows you to see literally at a glance what 